 average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.46\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.25 to +0.66), about +4.8\u00b0F since 1919.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 7 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"King Salmon's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.17 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 21.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1935 (31.55 in); the driest, 1959 (9.77 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 1 daily record high, 7 daily record lows"}}